Date: Tue, 9 Nov 2077 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Console ghost text suggestions

Adds an opt-in misc.console-ghost-text.enabled option that shows a
dimmed "ghost text" suggestion ahead of the console cursor as you
type, predicted from the closest match in console command history
(fish/zsh-shell style, via JLine's AutosuggestionWidgets). Accept
with Right arrow or End.

Only enabled when the console terminal is a real PTY that supports
ANSI escape codes; on a dumb terminal or a plain stdin/stdout pipe it
logs a warning on startup and leaves ghost text disabled instead,
unless misc.console-ghost-text.force-enable-on-unsupported-terminal
is set, in which case it force-enables anyway and warns that the
console output may look broken since the ANSI escape sequences won't
be interpreted by a terminal that doesn't support them.

